==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|paralepsis|paraleipsis}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|παράλειψις|t=omission}}, from {{m|grc|παραλείπω|t=I pass over}}, from {{m|grc|παρά|t=by, near}} + {{m|grc|λείπω|t=I leave}}.
{{root|en|ine-pro|*preh₂-}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpæ.ɹəˈlɪp.sɪs/|a=UK,US}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-paralipsis.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{examples|
* [[needless to say]]
* [[not to mention]]
* “I will not speak of my adversary's scandalous venality and rapacity, his brutal conduct, his treachery and malice”
}}
{{en-noun|~|paraleipses}}

# {{lb|en|rhetoric|linguistics}} A [[figure of speech]] in which one [[pretend]]s to [[ignore]] or [[omit]] something by actually [[mention]]ing it. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|apophasis|preterition}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1990|author=w:Camille Paglia|title=Sexual Personae
|passage=These negatives are a '''paraleipsis''': what cannot be done to the soul ''can'' be done to the body.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Alisa Lebow|title=First Person Jewish|page=60
|passage=Oxenberg tells us twice that she does not talk about the sister who died. She fools no one with this '''paralipsis''' {{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2 November 2016|journal=Slate
|passage=What's left to consider? I am loath to bring up Trump's '''paralipsis'''.}}

